A||||7||pHoOl||Manually shifting the Automatic||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||09-12-2000||10:33 AM||||Does anybody know if this is a problem?  I asked my mom who quite Hydromatic when i was born, and she didn't know.  I usually only do this when i'm clocking 0-60 and if i ever find a Mudstain that wants to race, i might do it then.  When i shift it manually i get higher rpm's out than when i just floor it and let it do it's thing.  Am i raping my trans by doing this?<P>I remember that there was a thread about this a while ago, but it never really had a good answer to it.  Any engineers on the board?<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||KnightRyder31||09-12-2000||10:45 AM||||No, as far as I know, there isn't anything wrong with doing this. Just as long as you don't rev your Fiero to high. I used to wonder about the same thing, but then I asked a Tranmission mechanic, and he told me that it wasn't a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-12-2000||06:00 PM||||Just don't try to downshift that way.  I did that once to a Chevy Monza (SBC, big wheels/tires, etc) and I broke the motor mounts and put the fan through the radiator.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||09-12-2000||06:09 PM||||You can downshift it manually without any problems.  You can shift it into L1 at 100MPH and it won't shift until the engine speed drops to the proper level.  The only thing you have to prepare for is the shift itself.  I like taking a sharp corner fast and downshift before I get there.....if I time it right it will kickdown to L1 right as I enter the curve and the rear end slides around perfectly.  If you aren't ready for the shift then it'll take you by surprise, so beware!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||pHoOl||09-13-2000||06:57 PM||||Sounds good guys, i'll just have to pretend i have a clutch now.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||09-13-2000||07:02 PM||||I can go from 60 to a dead stop in no time flat when I downshift.  At about 40 it shifts down to first and the rears squak and you are stoped!<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000006||Robert||09-13-2000||07:18 PM||||Are you guys saying that you can trough it into first gear while going 60MPH?  ||||reg||5
Z||000007||86SE||09-13-2000||11:03 PM||||You can drop it to first at 100, but the computer won't let it shift until about 45 MPH, but when it shifts and you have your foot on the brake, watch out, because the the rear tires HOOK UP!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention<p>[This message has been edited by 86SE (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
